# ── Telemetry data — NEVER commit ────────────────────────────────────────
# The InfluxDB CSV exports are far too large for git: the 10 files that were
# briefly committed came to 171 MB, and endurance_full.csv alone is 235 MB,
# which exceeds GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit outright. The data lives
# in the team's shared drive instead — see README.md for where to get it and
# where to put it.
comp2026_data/
*.csv

# parse_influx.py's pickled parse cache — regenerated automatically on first
# run of any case script (369 MB across the current data set).
*.parsed.pkl

# ── Generated analysis output — all reproducible by rerunning ─────────────
# plots/ is ~633 MB and contains individual HTML files over 100 MB (the
# endurance before/after plots), so it cannot be committed even in part.
plots/
filter_compare_results/

# ── Windows / editor cruft ───────────────────────────────────────────────
*:Zone.Identifier
*.Zone.Identifier

# ── Superseded exploratory work, kept locally only ───────────────────────
old - ignore/
